  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieved the best accuracy (0.5353), substantially outperforming both the RNA-only baseline (config_022, 0.4849) and the scgpt variant (config_004, 0.4348). This strongly suggests pca_n2000 is the superior RNA encoder and that adding the image modality via concat provides a meaningful gain. However, fusion strategy has only been tested as 'concat' so far. Question: config_005 is identical to config_002 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, cleanly isolating the effect of fusion strategy while holding RNA encoder, image encoder, and profile setting constant. Why this is best: With only 3 completed experiments, the evidence base is sparse. This single-variable comparison directly extends our best result and answers whether a more sophisticated fusion (weighted) can further improve on the promising pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l combination. If weighted fusion helps, it opens a high-value direction; if not, we confirm concat is sufficient and can redirect budget toward profile/aggregation questions. It avoids changing multiple factors simultaneously and is the most information-dense next step."
}

